New calculations for Fe I.   22 Oct 2014

NIST adopted newer wavelength standards that revise the wavelengths and
energy levels for Fe I.  See the atomic energy levels for Fe I on the 
NIST website.  All the energies have been updated.

The least squares fits have been revised many times, especially when
the line list predicted multiplets with lines with jumbled strengths or
lines in the wrong location compared to observed spectra.  These usually 
were because of interchanged levels.  Fiorella Castelli found several of 
these errors.

Ruth Peterson has identified 66 new levels:
                              
